  "name": "Teke zortlatması (Western Taurus Yörük dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Teke region of southwestern Anatolia around Burdur, Antalya and Isparta, rooted in its Yörük pastoralist communities. Its best-known form is the zortlatma, fast and vigorous men's dance tunes in aksak 9/8 played on the sipsi, a small single-reed cane pipe, together with the bağlama, alongside sung türkü; TRT recordings and Kalan Müzik regional anthologies document the repertoire.",
  "recipe": "classic modern teke zortlatması, wedding, middle eastern branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. sipsi, saz baglama. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
